senses.gloss:
--(शिवमन्दिरम्) Brahmalokam: the kingdom sacred to शिव; in distance a lac of yojanas from Brahmalokam; on the right was वैकुण्ठ and on the left, गौरीलोकम्; beyond was Dhruvalokam; here live पाशुपतस्; there are also the पारिजता and कामधेनु; विश्वकर्मा built it in a dream, set with golden gems; lion gate-way with two gate-keepers dressed in शिव garb; the सभा; शिव with five faces and ten hands surrounded by the Bhairavas and the Rudras besides the अष्टमूर्तिस्;
1: Br. III. ३१. ३४-9; Ch. ३२ (whole); ३४. ३२; वा. १११. ५४.
attained by one who makes a gift of the वायु Pura1n2am;
2: M. ५३. १९.
for observance of कृष्णाष्- टमि;
3: Ib. ५६. ११.
for bath in ऋषितीर्थम्.
4: Ib. ९२. २८; १९१. २२; १९२. ३८.

--by शुक्र;
1: M. ४७. १२८-68.
by Gods before the war against Tripura;
2: Ib. १३२. २१-28.
by Rati after Manmatha's death;
3: Ib. १५४. २६०. ७०.
by Munis when they went to request him to marry पार्वती;
4: Ib. १५४. ३९७. ४०४.
by बाण Asura;
5: Ib. १८८. ६३, ७१.
by भृगु (करुणाभ्युदय);
6: Ib. १९३. ३४-45.
by the Gods and Asuras at अमृतमथन (to swallow कालकूट),
7: Ib. २५०. २८-40.
by नारायण and ब्रह्मा.
8: वा. २४. ९०-165.
